  "texts": {
    "name": "Salvage",
    "blurb": "Drag a tether through matching debris and haul it in. Close the line into a loop to net every crate adrift.",
    "how_to": "Drag a line through touching debris of one kind, diagonals included, and let go to haul it: a line of n pieces scores n times n. Loot crates cannot be tethered. A crate that sinks to the floor is taken for a little; to take crates for what they are worth, bring the line back onto its first piece. A closed line is a net: it hauls every crate on the field at once, and crates are worth far more together than apart.",
    "stage.paths": "Lines",
    "stage.paths_intro": "Drag through touching debris of one kind and let go. The longer the line, the more each piece is worth.",
    "stage.streak": "Streak and crates",
    "stage.streak_intro": "Lines of five or more build a streak. Loot crates are adrift: dig under one to sink it to the floor.",
    "stage.loops": "Nets and orders",
    "stage.loops_intro": "Close a line onto its first piece to net every crate at once. Fill the order with one long line of its kind.",
    "stage.full": "Full salvage",
    "stage.full_intro": "Volatiles drift in. Defuse them late for more, but never let one burn out.",
